---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Structured on the HighLevel privacy policy at
 * https://www.gohighlevel.com/privacy-policy and rewritten for
 * Goal Green World Pte Ltd's operations as a Singapore painting and
 * waterproofing contractor, and for compliance with Singapore's
 * Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (the PDPA).
 *
 * Sections that were specific to HighLevel and do not apply here have
 * been removed, the EU/UK/US/Canadian/Australian rights sections
 * (GGW operates in Singapore), the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework
 * certification (GGW is not a party to it), and the processor-vs-controller
 * split from HighLevel's SaaS model (GGW is only ever the controller of
 * the personal data it collects through this site).
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import client from '../config/client.ts';

const { company, legal, contact } = client;
const address = [
  contact.address.line1,
  contact.address.line2,
  [contact.address.city, contact.address.postalCode].filter(Boolean).join(' '),
]
  .filter(Boolean)
  .join(', ');
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  intro={`How ${company.legalName} collects, uses, protects and shares your personal data.`}
>
  <h2>1. Overview</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName} (<strong>{company.registrationNumber}</strong>, “Goal
    Green World”, “we”, “us” and “our”) respects your privacy and is committed
    to protecting it through compliance with this Privacy Policy (the “Privacy
    Policy”). This Privacy Policy describes how we collect and use your
    Personal Data when you visit our website, communicate with us, or otherwise
    engage our painting and waterproofing services (collectively, the
    “Services”).
  </p>
  <p>
    In this Privacy Policy “Personal Data” has the meaning given to it in the
    Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (the “PDPA”): data, whether
    true or not, about an individual who can be identified from that data, or
    from that data and other information to which we have or are likely to have
    access.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please read this Privacy Policy to understand our policies and practices
    regarding your Personal Data and how we will handle it. If you do not agree
    with our policies and practices, do not use our Services. By accessing or
    using our Services, you agree and consent to this Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information That Goal Green World Collects About You</h2>
  <p>We collect information about you (“Personal Data”):</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Directly from you when you provide it to us.</strong> When you
      submit an enquiry, request a quotation, engage our Services, make a
      payment, subscribe to a newsletter or otherwise contact us, we will ask
      for things like your name, contact details (including email address,
      phone number and property address), billing and payment information, and
      the details of the project you are asking us to work on, in order to
      fulfil your request. If you submit any Personal Data about other people
      to us (for example your spouse, tenant, landlord or management
      corporation), you are responsible for making sure that you have the
      authority to do so and to allow us to use their Personal Data in
      accordance with this Privacy Policy (for example, by obtaining their
      consent).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>From third parties.</strong> We may obtain information about you
      through marketing partners and referrers (such as customers who refer
      you, advertising and marketing companies, and social media platforms) or
      other third parties (such as your management corporation, your landlord,
      publicly available business directories, or suppliers whose products you
      have asked us to install). This information can include, for example,
      your name, contact information and content that is publicly available.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatically when you use our Services.</strong> We collect
      information about how you interact with our website, including
      information about your device (such as your IP address and other technical
      information about your device), the actions you take on our website, and
      through the use of cookies, pixel tags, web beacons and similar
      technologies (collectively, “cookies”). This includes analytics and
      advertising measurement tools such as Google Analytics, the Meta pixel
      and Google Ads conversion tracking. You can control cookies through your
      browser settings; our website continues to function if you do so,
      although some conveniences may not work.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How Goal Green World Uses Information It Collects About You</h2>
  <p>
    We use Personal Data that we collect about you or that you provide to us
    for the following purposes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To provide and deliver our Services.</strong> We use your
      Personal Data to respond to your enquiry, prepare a quotation, schedule
      and carry out painting and waterproofing work, deliver materials, provide
      after-sales and warranty support, and otherwise perform the Services you
      have engaged us for.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For business operations.</strong> We use information to operate
      our business, for example to perform accounting, invoicing, auditing,
      billing, reconciliation, credit control and collection activities, and to
      comply with contractual obligations to our customers, suppliers and
      subcontractors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To communicate with you.</strong> We use contact information to
      send messages; to communicate with you about your project, your account
      and our Services; to respond to customer service requests; to send
      alerts such as scheduling updates or changes to our policies; and to send
      marketing or informational materials, in accordance with your
      communication preferences.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For customer support.</strong> We use your Personal Data to
      provide you with customer support, including warranty and post-completion
      support.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To protect and secure our website and business.</strong> We may
      use information to keep our Services safe, such as crime, fraud, and
      abuse monitoring and prevention, and cybersecurity efforts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For advertising and marketing.</strong> We may use Personal Data
      about you, including which pages you viewed and other information we
      collect, to enable us to provide personalised content, verify eligibility
      for and extend promotional offers, and study the effectiveness of our
      advertising and marketing campaigns. We use analytics data from our
      website and from marketing partners to measure how well our advertising
      is working. Where required by law we will obtain your consent before
      sending you marketing communications, and you may withdraw that consent
      at any time (see Section 10).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For statistical purposes to improve our Services.</strong> We
      compile statistics about how our website is used, which helps us
      understand, anticipate and respond to what our customers need. This
      information helps us create a better overall experience for our
      customers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For legal, regulatory and compliance purposes.</strong> We may
      use Personal Data to comply with legal, regulatory or related
      obligations, including to protect our legal rights.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis for our use.</strong> Under the PDPA, we collect, use
    and disclose your Personal Data on one of the following bases: (a) with
    your consent (which may be given expressly or, where permitted by the
    PDPA, deemed by conduct such as voluntarily providing your Personal Data
    for an obvious purpose); (b) where the collection, use or disclosure is
    necessary for the performance of a contract with you or to take steps at
    your request before entering into a contract; (c) where the collection,
    use or disclosure is required or authorised by law; or (d) where the PDPA
    otherwise permits (including where the collection, use or disclosure is in
    our legitimate interests and a reasonable person would consider it
    appropriate in the circumstances).
  </p>
  <p>
    If we ask you to provide Personal Data to comply with a legal requirement
    or to perform a contract with you, we will make this clear at the time of
    collection. We will also tell you whether the requirement for that
    information is mandatory and explain any consequences to you if you do not
    provide the information.
  </p>
  <p>
    Goal Green World is the data controller of all Personal Data collected
    through our website and Services. If you have questions about, or need
    further information concerning, the legal basis on which we collect and
    use your Personal Data for any specific processing activity, please contact
    us using the details provided under Section 14 (“How to Contact Us”).
  </p>

  <h2>4. How Goal Green World Protects Your Information</h2>
  <p>
    We design our website and business processes to provide reasonable and
    appropriate administrative, technical and organisational security measures
    to protect your Personal Data against risks such as temporary or permanent
    loss, destruction, and unauthorised or unlawful access, alteration, use or
    disclosure. These measures include access controls on our business
    systems, transport encryption for information submitted through our
    website, and contractual obligations on our suppliers and vendors to apply
    similar protections when they access or use Personal Data that we share
    with them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Users of our website and Services must also do their part in protecting
    their data, systems, networks and the services they are utilising. No
    technology, data transmission or system can be guaranteed to be 100%
    secure. If you have reason to believe that your interaction with us is no
    longer secure, please immediately notify us by contacting us using the
    instructions in Section 14 (“How to Contact Us”).
  </p>

  <h2>5. When Goal Green World Shares Your Information</h2>
  <p>
    We may disclose Personal Data with the following categories of third
    parties:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>With service providers acting on our behalf.</strong> We may
      share information with our authorised vendors and suppliers to provide
      services we have contracted for, such as website hosting, customer
      relationship management, data analysis, IT services, auditing, accounting
      and customer service. Our contracts with these service providers include
      provisions to protect your Personal Data and limit its use to the
      services we have engaged them to provide.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With trade partners engaged for your project.</strong> We may
      share information with scaffolders, product suppliers or specialist
      subcontractors we engage to complete work you have asked us to do, and
      only to the extent needed to complete that work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With marketing partners.</strong> We share your information with
      our advertising and analytics providers to measure and improve the
      effectiveness of our marketing, and in some cases to prepare and deliver
      advertising content to relevant audiences. We do not sell your Personal
      Data. For information about how to manage our advertising and marketing,
      please see Section 10.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With third-party services you connect to.</strong> If you connect
      third-party services to our Services, for example if you communicate
      with us through WhatsApp or Facebook Messenger, you are agreeing to
      provide information about you to those third-party services under their
      respective terms and privacy policies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sales, mergers and acquisitions.</strong> We may disclose
      Personal Data as part of a contemplated or actual corporate transaction
      such as a reorganisation, merger, sale, joint venture, assignment,
      transfer or other disposition of all or any portion of our business,
      assets or shares (including in connection with any insolvency or similar
      proceedings), subject to equivalent protections continuing to apply to
      your Personal Data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For legal, regulatory or related purposes.</strong> We may
      disclose your information to the extent required by law or if we have a
      good-faith belief that such disclosure is necessary in order to comply
      with official investigations or legal proceedings initiated by
      governmental or law enforcement officials, or private parties, including
      but not limited to in response to subpoenas, search warrants, court
      orders or written requests from the Personal Data Protection Commission
      of Singapore (the “PDPC”).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At your direction or with your consent.</strong> Goal Green World
      may disclose your Personal Data to any other person or entity where you
      consent to the disclosure or otherwise direct us to disclose the
      information.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not share your phone number, SMS or WhatsApp originator opt-in data,
    or consent with any third parties, excluding aggregators and providers of
    the messaging services we use to send those messages to you.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We will only retain your Personal Data for as long as reasonably necessary
    to fulfil the purposes we collected it for, including for the purposes of
    satisfying any legal, regulatory, tax, accounting, warranty or reporting
    requirements and for other purposes described in this Privacy Policy. We
    may retain your Personal Data for a longer period in the event of a
    complaint or if we reasonably believe there is a prospect of litigation in
    respect to our relationship with you.
  </p>
  <p>
    To determine the appropriate retention period for Personal Data, we
    consider the amount, nature and sensitivity of the Personal Data, the
    potential risk of harm from unauthorised use or disclosure of your
    Personal Data, the purposes for which we process your Personal Data and
    whether we can achieve those purposes through other means, and the
    applicable legal, regulatory, tax, accounting or other requirements. In
    some circumstances you can ask us to delete your data (see Section 10). In
    some circumstances we will anonymise your Personal Data (so that it can no
    longer be associated with you) for research or statistical purposes, in
    which case we may use this information indefinitely without further notice
    to you.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Information From Children</h2>
  <p>
    We do not knowingly collect, use, disclose, sell, or share Personal Data
    from children under 13. If we learn that we have collected the Personal
    Data of a child under 13 we will take steps to delete the information as
    soon as possible. If you are under 13, do not provide any information about
    yourself to Goal Green World, including your name, address, telephone
    number or email address. If you become aware that Personal Data of a child
    under 13 has been provided to us, please let us know using one of the
    methods provided in Section 14 (“How to Contact Us”).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Links to Other Websites and Services</h2>
  <p>
    We are not responsible for the practices employed by websites or services
    linked to or from our Services, including the information or content
    contained therein. This Privacy Policy does not address, and we are not
    responsible for, the policies and practices of third parties or other
    organisations that are not operating on Goal Green World’s behalf,
    including policies and practices related to privacy and security, data
    collection, processing, use, storage, and disclosure. This includes any
    third party operating any site or service to which our Services link, the
    inclusion of a link on our Services does not imply endorsement of the
    linked site or service by us, and any app developer, app provider, social
    media platform provider, operating system provider, wireless service
    provider or device manufacturer, including any Personal Data you disclose
    to other organisations through or in connection with our Services.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    Some browsers incorporate a “Do Not Track” (“DNT”) feature that, when
    turned on, signals to websites and online services that you do not want to
    be tracked. At this time, our Services do not respond to DNT signals.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your Legal Rights Under the Singapore PDPA</h2>
  <p>
    Goal Green World respects your rights related to your Personal Data. The
    PDPA gives you the following rights in respect of Personal Data we hold
    about you.
  </p>

  <h3>Right of access</h3>
  <p>
    You may request confirmation of the Personal Data we hold about you, and
    information about the ways in which that Personal Data has been used or
    disclosed by us during the year before the date of your request. You can
    make such a request by writing to our Data Protection Officer using the
    details in Section 14 (“How to Contact Us”). We may charge a reasonable
    fee to fulfil your request, as permitted by the PDPA, and we may require
    evidence of your identity before doing so.
  </p>

  <h3>Right of correction</h3>
  <p>
    You may request that we correct an error or omission in the Personal Data
    that we hold about you. You can make such a request by writing to our Data
    Protection Officer using the details in Section 14. Once we correct your
    Personal Data we will, unless you have told us otherwise, send the
    corrected data to every other organisation to which we disclosed that
    Personal Data in the year before the date of the correction.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to withdraw consent</h3>
  <p>
    Where we have collected your Personal Data with your consent, you can
    withdraw that consent at any time. You can do so by writing to our Data
    Protection Officer using the details in Section 14, or, for marketing SMS
    and WhatsApp messages, by replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any such
    message.
  </p>
  <p>
    Withdrawing your consent will not affect (a) the lawfulness of any
    processing we conducted prior to your withdrawal, or (b) processing your
    Personal Data under other legal bases. Withdrawing your consent may limit
    our ability to respond to your enquiry, complete work you have engaged us
    for, or provide warranty support, we will let you know the specific
    consequences at the time.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to be informed</h3>
  <p>
    You have the right to be informed of the purposes for which your Personal
    Data is being collected, used or disclosed on or before those activities
    take place. This Privacy Policy is intended to satisfy that requirement.
  </p>

  <h3>Right to complain</h3>
  <p>
    If you believe we are using your Personal Data in a way that is
    inconsistent with this Privacy Policy or with the PDPA, please contact us
    using the details in Section 14. If we cannot resolve your complaint, you
    have the right to lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection
    Commission of Singapore at{' '}
    <a href="https://www.pdpc.gov.sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      www.pdpc.gov.sg
    </a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Advertising and marketing choices</h3>
  <p>
    To exercise your choices regarding our use and disclosure of your Personal
    Data for advertising and marketing purposes, you may update your
    communication preferences or opt out by using one of the methods in
    Section 14. Please note that if you choose not to receive marketing
    communications from us, we may still send you communications related to
    your project or account, such as scheduling information, warranty notices
    or service issues.
  </p>

  <h2>11. International Data Transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of the service providers we use, for example our email provider,
    our website host and our customer relationship management platform, process Personal Data on servers located outside Singapore. Where we
    transfer Personal Data out of Singapore, we take reasonable steps required
    by the PDPA to ensure that the recipient is bound by legally enforceable
    obligations to provide a standard of protection at least comparable to
    that under the PDPA. In practice this is achieved through contractual
    clauses in our vendor agreements, and (where applicable) by relying on
    binding corporate rules of the recipient organisation.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Privacy Policy Updates</h2>
  <p>
    Goal Green World may change this Privacy Policy at any time, at its
    discretion. We will revise the “last updated” date at the top of this page
    when we do. Where the changes are material, we will take reasonable steps
    to notify you. Your continued use of our Services after we make changes is
    deemed to be acceptance of and consent to those changes, so please check
    the Privacy Policy periodically for updates.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Data Protection Officer</h2>
  <p>
    In accordance with Section 11(3) of the PDPA, we have appointed a Data
    Protection Officer to oversee compliance with this Privacy Policy and the
    PDPA. All requests to access, correct or withdraw consent for your
    Personal Data, and all complaints and other queries about how we handle
    your Personal Data, should be directed to our Data Protection Officer.
  </p>

  <h2>14. How to Contact Us About This Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>
    To ask questions about this Privacy Policy and our privacy practices, or
    to exercise any of your rights under Section 10, contact our Data
    Protection Officer at:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Data Protection Officer</strong><br />
    {company.legalName} ({company.registrationNumber})<br />
    {address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.privacyEmail}`}>{legal.privacyEmail}</a><br />
    Telephone: <a href={`tel:${contact.phoneHref}`}>{contact.phone}</a>
  </p>

  <p>
    In compliance with the Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012, {company.legalName} commits to resolve PDPA-related complaints about our collection and use of your personal data. Individuals in Singapore with inquiries or complaints regarding our handling of personal data under the PDPA should first contact {company.name} at: <a href={`mailto:${legal.privacyEmail}`}>{legal.privacyEmail}</a>. If we are unable to resolve your complaint within a reasonable time, you may lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection Commission of Singapore at <a href="https://www.pdpc.gov.sg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.pdpc.gov.sg</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
